{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The fix is applied and submitted. The submission endpoint returned 200.\n\n**Root cause:** Postgres rejected logins for the `otelu` user. Every service that uses it (`product-catalog`, `product-reviews`, `accounting`, and `recommendation` through `product-catalog`) sends the same password, `otelp_7k9m2q4x`. The password stored in the database for `otelu` was different, so `product-catalog` couldn't load products. Users saw \"Product Not Found\" errors in the frontend.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the password on the `otelu` role to `otelp_7k9m2q4x`. I did this with `ALTER USER` as `root`. I then restarted `product-catalog`, `recommendation`, `accounting` and `product-reviews`.\n\n**Check:** `otelu` can now query `catalog.products`, `reviews.productreviews` and `accounting.order`. After the restarts, the last 30 seconds of logs showed no Postgres auth failures and no frontend \"Not Found\" errors. All pods are Running."}}
